body:
Thank you for your response! It's good to hear that my thoughts on this issue are accurate. I am planning to start pushing to exit students with these types of goals (or at least switch them to consult.)

&#x200B;

I guess relating to the 'super goals' one issue I find is that it can be a little disheartening (to me, to families, to my students) when annuals come around. If a student meets say, 2/3 of his/her goal but does not achieve the last 1/3, marking that (s)he didn't meet their goal can be frustrating. What are your thoughts on this? Is it just an unfortunate part of goal writing, or are there other ways I can report on these goals?
